<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aboriginal Tasmanians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Palawa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aboriginal Tasmanians are the Indigenous people of Tasmania, isolated from the mainland when rising seas formed Bass Strait about 10,000 years ago. Numbering several thousand at British settlement in 1803, they were devastated by violence, disease and dispossession, especially in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-war">Black War</a> of the 1820s, and the survivors were removed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flinders-island">Flinders Island</a>. Their descendants, many from the Bass Strait islands, form today's Tasmanian Aboriginal community.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aboriginal-tasmanians.jpg" alt="Aboriginal Tasmanians" width="320" height="518" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benjamin Duterrau (1768–1851) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Last_of_the_Tasmanians_Woodcut_6_-_Wooreddy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
